Subject: [PATCH] net: ppe: disable unsafe bridge TX forwarding offload

The bridge marks known unicast as well as flooded traffic for TX forwarding
offload. EDMA treats either mark as a request for bitmap replication, sending
FDB-hit unicast to unrelated ports. Multicast MDB destinations can likewise
be replaced by the generic flood bitmap.

Keep switchdev bridge registration and hardware forwarding, but decline TX
forwarding offload for every port. Linux must retain per-port cloning for
unknown unicast and multicast; merely ignoring the mark in EDMA would lose
copies already suppressed by the bridge's hardware-domain tracking.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
@@ -894,15 +894,15 @@
 
 	ppe_bridge_port_offload_mark_set(dev, true);
 
-	/* On a VLAN-unaware bridge every replication target receives
-	 * the identical frame, so the bridge may hand over a single
-	 * copy of flooded packets. VLAN-aware bridges keep cloning in
-	 * software, their egress tagging differs per port.
+	/* offload_fwd_mark also marks FDB-hit unicast, not just flooding.
+	 * EDMA cannot distinguish those cases and would send known unicast
+	 * to the entire UC flood bitmap. Keep hardware bridge offload, but
+	 * let the bridge select and clone each software TX destination.
 	 */
 	ret = switchdev_bridge_port_offload(dev, dev, pb,
 					    &pb->switchdev_nb,
 					    &pb->switchdev_blocking_nb,
-					    !vlan_aware, extack);
+					    false, extack);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_offload;
 
